CONTEXT
    Select only the exact path supplied by the user or recorded in this conversation
    for the canonical project, Jira ticket, and draft kind. Reject mismatches or
    ambiguous selection; never scan temporary directories or infer a ticket from a
    filename. Ask for missing selection details. Read developer edits on every action.
    Writing may create a new draft only when none is known; a known missing file is
    an error. Refine, improve, explain, publish, and done require an existing draft.

    Create only the requested pr.md or technical-summary.md in a unique private OS
    temporary directory outside the canonical project, resolving paths and symlinks.
    Use 0700 directory and 0600 file permissions where supported. Allocate only when
    the draft is ready. Record the absolute path, project, ticket, kind, and directory
    ownership in conversation context. Create no repository task files or registry.
    Before saving or publishing, verify task identity and the current file still
    match the identity and text read for this action. Stop on concurrent edits.

    Keep Markdown after writing and failed or uncertain publication. After verified
    publication, remove only the selected file if it still matches the published text.
    Explicit done may remove an incomplete selected draft without publishing or Jira,
    Git readiness, or tool checks. Never follow links. Remove only an empty directory
    owned by this workflow; forget only the cleaned record. Preserve other drafts and
    report cleanup failures or retained paths. A new task does not clean old drafts.
AS draft_rules
